Z||000000||theogre||03-24-2001||12:09 AM||||The brake upgrade article is now posted in what is likely it's final form. A number of links have been added and various things cleaned up. Most of it should make sense now. It should also load faster. (I cleaned out 34K worth of inline styles that Word2k stuffed in it.)<P>several other articles have had minor corrections/changes.<P>At this point I'm about done with most of the things I plane to add to the cave. I'm doing a small article about resurecting the visors. It may have patterns for making new covers. <P>Other than that I can't think of much else to add to it. If anyone has ideas let me know. I'm going to have surgury in may. I'll need something to keep me busy for 4-8 weeks.<P>WebTV indexes have not been updated. I'll get to those next week.<P>IE Channel is no longer actively supported. It's to much of a pain in the a__ and no one seems to bother to use it. (No, IE 5.x can't read the site for offline use. The script menus don't allow it. The channel is the only way to use the majority of the site off line.)||||reg||7
